messages.content:
Requirements (JSON records in document order; dependencies list the prerequisite requirement ids):
[
{
"id": "ROOT",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Keep",
"description": "Note management system for creating, organizing, searching, and configuring personal notes.",
"dependencies": []
},
{
"id": "REQ-1",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Google Keep Home Page",
"description": "Main workspace of the application. It shows the notes area, pinned notes section, header actions, search entry, settings entry, sidebar navigation, and quick label access. Reference image:",
"dependencies": [],
"parent": "ROOT"
},
{
"id": "REQ-1.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Enter Website",
"description": "Open the application and display the home page. The page exposes a visible region named `Notes workspace`, a button named `Take a note`, and a textbox named `Search`.",
"dependencies": [],
"parent": "REQ-1",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Enter Website",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User has a browser or app with network access.",
"WHEN: Open the application entry URL.",
"THEN: The home page is displayed with the `Notes workspace` region, the `Take a note` button, and the `Search` textbox visible."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Notes Management",
"description": "Core note management capability for listing, creating, updating, deleting, archiving, coloring, labeling, and pinning notes. Reference image:",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-1"
],
"parent": "ROOT"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Note Listing",
"description": "Display the notes list on the home page with pinned notes shown separately from unpinned notes. The pinned section is a named region or heading `Pinned`, and the regular section is a named region or heading `Others`. Each note is exposed as a unique article named by its title. Seed data: pinned note \"Sprint goals\" and regular note \"Groceries\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-1.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Note Listing",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User has opened the application and the system is accessible.",
"WHEN: View the home page.",
"THEN: The page displays visible `Pinned` and `Others` sections, with `Sprint goals` in the pinned section and `Groceries` in the regular section."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Create Note",
"description": "Create a note from the `Take a note` button. Activating it opens exactly one dialog named `Note editor` containing uniquely labelled textboxes `Title` and `Note content`, plus a button named `Close`. Closing the dialog autosaves the note. Take a note form from homepage image: Note form image:",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Create Note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique button `Take a note`, fill the `Title` textbox with `Weekend plan`, fill the `Note content` textbox with `Visit the farmers market and prep lunches.`, and activate the `Close` button in the `Note editor` dialog.",
"THEN: The `Note editor` dialog closes, the note is autosaved, and exactly one note article named `Weekend plan` appears in the notes list."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.3",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Delete Note",
"description": "Delete notes from the note actions menu and manage the deleted-note recovery flow.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.3.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Delete",
"description": "Delete a note from its actions without an extra confirmation dialog. Each note is an article containing a button named `More options`; activating it exposes a button named `Delete Note` scoped to that note. Deletion exposes a status message `Note trashed` and a button named `Undo`. Dropdown image: Seed data: deletable note \"Delete me 2.3.1\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.3",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Delete",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see at least one note.",
"WHEN: Hover over the article for `Delete me 2.3.1`, activate its `More options` button, and activate its `Delete Note` button.",
"THEN: The `Delete me 2.3.1` article is absent from the main notes list, a visible status message displays exactly `Note trashed`, and a unique button named `Undo` is available."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.3.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Notification and Undo",
"description": "Show a delete status notification with a unique `Undo` button after a note is deleted. Activating `Undo` restores the same note article and displays a status message exactly `Action undone`. Reference image for notification: Seed data: deletable note \"Delete me 2.3.2\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.3.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.3",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Notification and Undo",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User has just deleted a note from the home page.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Undo` button in the visible delete notification.",
"THEN: The `Delete me 2.3.2` note article is restored and the page shows a visible status message exactly `Action undone`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.3.3",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Trash list",
"description": "Open the Trash view from the sidebar and display deleted notes. The sidebar is exposed as a complementary landmark and contains a unique button named `Trash`. Reference image: Seed data: deletable note \"Delete me 2.3.3\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.3.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.3",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Trash list",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User can see the sidebar.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique button named `Trash` in the sidebar.",
"THEN: The Trash view displays the deleted note article named `Delete me 2.3.3`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.4",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Update Note",
"description": "Edit the content of an existing note and persist it after closing the editor. Activating the note article opens a dialog named `Note editor` containing a textbox named `Note content` and a button named `Close`. Reference image: Seed data: note \"Project ideas\" with initial content \"Initial editable content\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Update Note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see a note.",
"WHEN: Open the `Project ideas` note article, replace `Note content` with `Updated editable content for the note editor.`, and activate `Close`.",
"THEN: The `Note editor` dialog closes and the `Project ideas` article displays `Updated editable content for the note editor.`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.5",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Archive Note",
"description": "Archive and unarchive notes, and show the archived notes list separately from active notes.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.5.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Archive",
"description": "Archive a note using the button named `Archive` inside its note article and show a status message exactly `Note archived` with a unique `Undo` button. Reference image: Seed data: active note \"Travel plans 2.5.1\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.5",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Archive",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see a note.",
"WHEN: Activate the `Archive` button inside the `Travel plans 2.5.1` note article.",
"THEN: The note is absent from the main list, is stored in the archive list, and the page shows `Note archived` with a unique `Undo` button."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.5.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Archive Undo",
"description": "Restore an archived note by using the Undo action from the archive notification. Seed data: active note \"Travel plans 2.5.2\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.5.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.5",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Archive Undo",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: The archive notification is visible after archiving a note.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Undo` button in the archive notification.",
"THEN: The note article named `Travel plans 2.5.2` returns to the main notes list."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.5.3",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Show archived notes",
"description": "Open the Archive view from the sidebar using the unique button named `Archive` and display archived note articles. Reference image: Seed data: active note \"Travel plans 2.5.3\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.5.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.5",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Show archived notes",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User can see the sidebar.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Archive` button in the sidebar.",
"THEN: The Archive view displays the note article named `Travel plans 2.5.3`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.5.4",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Unarchive",
"description": "Restore an archived note using the button named `Unarchive` inside its note article. Reference image: Seed data: active note \"Travel plans 2.5.4\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.5.3"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.5",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Unarchive",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is viewing the archived notes list.",
"WHEN: Activate the `Unarchive` button inside the `Travel plans 2.5.4` article.",
"THEN: The note is absent from the archived list and the `Travel plans 2.5.4` article is present in the main notes list."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.6",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Note Coloring",
"description": "Allow users to apply different background colors to notes during creation and after a note already exists. Reference image:",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.6.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Change note color",
"description": "Change the color of an existing note using its `Change color` button and a color button named `Light green`. Light green is represented by computed background color `rgb(204, 255, 144)`. Seed data: regular note \"Garden tasks existing\" with a white background.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.6",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Change note color",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see a note.",
"WHEN: Activate `Change color` in the `Garden tasks existing` article and activate the color button named `Light green`.",
"THEN: The note article background changes to computed color `rgb(204, 255, 144)`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.6.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Choose note color when created",
"description": "Set the color of a note during creation using the `Change color` and `Light green` buttons in the `Note editor` dialog.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.6",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Choose note color when created",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User has opened the \"Take a note\" editor.",
"WHEN: Activate `Change color`, activate `Light green`, fill `Title` with `Garden tasks created`, fill `Note content` with `Color me later`, and activate `Close`.",
"THEN: The `Garden tasks created` note article is saved with computed background color `rgb(204, 255, 144)`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Labels Management",
"description": "Allow users to assign labels to notes, manage labels, and filter notes by label.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Assign label to a note",
"description": "Assign labels to an existing note. The note article has a `More options` button; its menu has a `Change labels` button; the label editor exposes a checkbox named `Work`. Reference image: Seed data: regular note \"Team retro add label\" without the \"Work\" label; label \"Work\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Assign label to a note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see a note.",
"WHEN: In the `Team retro add label` article, activate `More options`, activate `Change labels`, check the `Work` checkbox, and activate `Close`.",
"THEN: The `Work` label is assigned and displayed inside the target note article."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Remove label from a note",
"description": "Remove an assigned label from a note. The note article exposes `More options` and `Change labels`; the label editor exposes a checked checkbox named `Work` and a `Close` button. Seed data: regular note \"Team retro remove label\" with the \"Work\" label; label \"Work\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Remove label from a note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see a note that already has a label.",
"WHEN: In the `Team retro remove label` article, activate `More options`, activate `Change labels`, uncheck `Work`, and activate `Close`.",
"THEN: The `Work` label is absent from the target note article; other notes and the sidebar remain unchanged."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.3",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Default label",
"description": "Provide `Reminders` as a default label in the sidebar. The sidebar exposes it as a unique button named `Reminders`. Seed data: default label \"Reminders\".",
"dependencies": [],
"parent": "REQ-2.7",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Default label",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: The system has been initialized.",
"WHEN: View the labels list.",
"THEN: The sidebar includes a unique button named `Reminders`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.4",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Assign default label when creating note",
"description": "Assign the default \"Reminders\" label during note creation. Seed data: default label \"Reminders\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.3"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Assign default label when creating note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and the \"Take a note\" editor is open.",
"WHEN: Open \"More options\", choose \"Change labels\", select the \"Reminders\" label, enter a title and content, and click \"Close\".",
"THEN: The created note is saved with the \"Reminders\" label."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.5",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Edit labels",
"description": "Create, rename, and delete labels from the label management list. Each label row is a named group, for example `Label Work editable`, containing a textbox labelled `Label Work editable` and a unique `Save` button. Reference image: Seed data: editable label \"Work editable\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Edit labels",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User can see the sidebar.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Edit labels` sidebar button, replace the `Label Work editable` textbox value with `Projects`, and activate its `Save` button.",
"THEN: The label list contains a textbox named `Label Projects`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.6",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "View by labels",
"description": "Show all labels in the sidebar and allow users to filter the notes list by the selected label. Reference image:",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.6.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "View list filtered by label",
"description": "Filter the notes list by a selected label. The sidebar exposes the label as a unique button named `Work`. Seed data: note \"Design review\" with the \"Work\" label and note \"Movie list\" without the \"Work\" or \"Reminders\" label; label \"Work\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7.6",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "View list filtered by label",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User can see the sidebar.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Work` button in the sidebar.",
"THEN: The notes list contains `Design review` and does not contain `Movie list`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.6.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "View all notes",
"description": "Return from a label-filtered view to the full notes list. Seed data: note \"Design review\" with the \"Work\" label and note \"Movie list\" without the \"Work\" or \"Reminders\" label; label \"Work\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.6.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7.6",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "View all notes",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User can see the sidebar.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Notes` button in the sidebar.",
"THEN: The notes list contains both `Design review` and `Movie list`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.7.6.3",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "View Reminders",
"description": "Filter the notes list by the default \"Reminders\" label. Seed data: note \"Call dentist existing\" with the \"Reminders\" label and note \"Movie list\" without the \"Work\" or \"Reminders\" label; label \"Reminders\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.7.3"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.7.6",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "View Reminders",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User can see the sidebar.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Reminders` button in the sidebar.",
"THEN: The notes list contains `Call dentist existing` and does not contain `Movie list`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.8",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Pinned Notes",
"description": "Allow users to pin frequently used notes to the top of the notes list and unpin them later.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2"
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.8.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Pin note",
"description": "Pin an existing note from its article using a button named `Pin note`. The pinned article exposes a title attribute `Pinned`. Reference image: Seed data: regular note \"Meeting agenda 2.8.1\" that is not pinned.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.8",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Pin note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and can see a note.",
"WHEN: Activate the `Pin note` button inside the `Meeting agenda 2.8.1` article.",
"THEN: The article has title `Pinned` and appears in the `Pinned` section."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.8.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Unpin note",
"description": "Remove the pinned state from a pinned note using its `Unpin note` button. The article no longer exposes title `Pinned`. Seed data: regular note \"Meeting agenda 2.8.2\" that is not pinned.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.8.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.8",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Unpin note",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and the note is pinned.",
"WHEN: Activate the `Unpin note` button inside the `Meeting agenda 2.8.2` article.",
"THEN: The article is absent from the pinned section, is present in the regular notes list, and has no `Pinned` title."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-2.8.3",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Pin note when creating it",
"description": "Create a note in the pinned state. The `Note editor` dialog contains a button named `Pin note` and a button named `Close`.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2.2"
],
"parent": "REQ-2.8",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Pin note when creating it",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and the \"Take a note\" editor is open.",
"WHEN: Fill `Title` with `Meeting agenda created`, fill `Note content` with `Pin this note`, activate `Pin note`, and activate `Close`.",
"THEN: The `Meeting agenda created` article is displayed in `Pinned` and exposes title `Pinned`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-3",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Search",
"description": "Allow users to search notes by keywords and supported filters.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2"
],
"parent": "ROOT"
},
{
"id": "REQ-3.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Initial suggested filters",
"description": "Show suggested search filters after the textbox named `Search` is focused. The suggestions are exposed as a listbox containing a button named `Reminders`; activating it filters the notes list. Image reference: Seed data: note \"Call dentist existing\" with the \"Reminders\" label; label \"Reminders\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-1.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-3",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Initial suggested filters",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page.",
"WHEN: Focus the `Search` textbox and activate the `Reminders` button in the visible suggestions listbox.",
"THEN: The notes list contains `Call dentist existing`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-3.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Search by keyword",
"description": "Search notes by keyword and highlight matching text in the results. The search control is a textbox named `Search`; matching occurrences are exposed in `mark` elements. Image reference: Seed data: note \"Study schedule\" whose title or content contains the keyword \"st\".",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-3.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-3",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Search by keyword",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page.",
"WHEN: Fill the `Search` textbox with `st`.",
"THEN: The notes list contains `Study schedule` and at least one `mark` element contains `st`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-4",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Settings",
"description": "Allow users to manage common application settings.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2"
],
"parent": "ROOT"
},
{
"id": "REQ-4.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Setting options list",
"description": "Display the settings options menu from a unique button named `Settings`. The opened menu has role `menu` and contains unique menuitems named `Settings`, `Help & feedback`, and `Send feedback`. Reference image:",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-1.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-4",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Setting options list",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Settings` button.",
"THEN: A visible `menu` displays menuitems `Settings`, `Help & feedback`, and `Send feedback`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-4.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Detailed settings",
"description": "Open the detailed settings page and display visible controls or text for `Move new notes to the bottom`, `Move checked items to the bottom`, `Save`, and `Cancel`.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-4.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-4",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Detailed settings",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page and the settings options list is visible.",
"WHEN: Activate the unique `Settings` menuitem.",
"THEN: The detailed settings page displays `Move new notes to the bottom`, `Move checked items to the bottom`, and unique controls named `Save` and `Cancel`."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-5",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "List View & Grid View",
"description": "Allow users to switch between grid view and list view for notes. Reference image for list view:",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-2"
],
"parent": "ROOT"
},
{
"id": "REQ-5.1",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Toggle between list and grid views",
"description": "Switch between list view and grid view from the home page toolbar. The toolbar contains buttons named `List view` and `Grid view`; exactly one has aria-pressed=true at a time.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-1.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-5",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Toggle between list and grid views",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User is on the home page.",
"WHEN: Activate `List view` and then activate `Grid view`.",
"THEN: `List view` has aria-pressed=true after the first activation; `Grid view` has aria-pressed=true after the second activation."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-5.2",
"type": "ATOMIC",
"name": "Grid View by default",
"description": "Display notes in grid view by default when the home page first loads. The `List view` button has aria-pressed=false and the `Grid view` button has aria-pressed=true.",
"dependencies": [
"REQ-1.1"
],
"parent": "REQ-5",
"scenarios": [
{
"name": "Grid View by default",
"steps": [
"GIVEN: User has a browser or app with network access.",
"WHEN: Open the application entry URL.",
"THEN: The notes page opens in grid view; `List view` has aria-pressed=false and `Grid view` has aria-pressed=true."
]
}
]
},
{
"id": "REQ-6",
"type": "FOLDER",
"name": "Sidebar",
"description": "Sidebar for common navigation actions such as notes, labels, archive, and trash.",
"dependencies": [
